    "text": "The most sensitive part, the Saudi purchases of American debt, was kept quiet. For more than four decades, the Treasury hid exactly how much Saudi Arabia held, by lumping it together with other oil exporters. The number only came out in twenty sixteen, after a news investigation and a records request. By then, the kingdom held over one hundred and sixteen billion dollars of U.S. government debt.",
